{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate","id":1559296,"title":"Is there a way to rehabilitate The Syndicate?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-08T16:54:39-07:00","id":1559296,"title":"Is there a way to rehabilitate The Syndicate?","content":"This question is not new around the forum, from what I could gather. I saw a post titled &quot;Heroic Syndicate (or at least decent) characters?&quot; which tackles somewhat what I'm gonna talk about here, with the difference that what I'm not tackling the issue from a character-level but in a convention/metaplot-level.<br /> <br /> The issue of corruption in the Technocracy is not new to M20, even though the creation of the Disparate Alliance gives renewed focus to this particular aspect of the metaplot. For reasons of better focusing the discussion and because the other two options makes the question itself completely irrelevant, I'm gonna (personally) assume the following metaplot option as true, from <i>M20 Corebook</i> (p.170):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>There\u2019s corruption, but they\u2019re dealing with it</b>: Yes, some Nephandi have warped the Union\u2019s purpose. And<br /> yeah, the Technocracy\u2019s brutal. But still, the Union can be saved. Devoted Technocrats \u2013 inspired and sometimes<br /> led by Secret Agent John Courage \u2013 have been fighting a covert war within the Technocracy\u2026 and despite major<br /> losses and obstacles, there\u2019s still hope for the Technocracy\u2019s redemption. </div> </div> </div>Alright, so going into a convention-to-convention basis, I can see how each one could be redeemed considering both how the Technocracy is handled in the Convention Books and in <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i>. Make the NWO less fascist, make Iteration X more accepting of chaos and human imperfection, make the Progenitors less of alienated mad scientists and make the Void Engineers less of a cosmic border patrol and focus on the ideal of exploring the universe. Of course, I'm simplifying <b>a lot</b>, but the point is I can see each of these conventions with a &quot;core good&quot; of sorts that would pave its way for rehabilitation, be it institutional stability (NWO) or ecological preservation (Progenitors).<br /> <br /> I cannot see a way to redeem the Syndicate. I can see a minority of heroic Syndicate agents, per the above mentioned post, but not a way to see this ideal being applied to the convention as a whole in a new Technocracy. Maybe it's my bias, given the current state of the world, but when I open the <i>Convention Book: Syndicate (Revised)</i> and see terms like &quot;Guardians of the Status Quo&quot; or &quot;The Syndicate is about the almighty Bottom Line&quot; or &quot;everything is for sale, one way or another (this one is in the <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i>)&quot;, I get this visceral reaction of &quot;right, these are the forever antagonists of this game, right there with the Nephandi&quot;. It doesn't help when I see the section of <i>The Book of Secrets</i> &quot;Technocratic Influence Upon The Masses&quot; and read this (p.230):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Certain groups have their pet projects too \u2013 the space program for<br /> Void Engineers,<b> endless indulgence for the Syndicate</b>, fear of<br /> The Other for the NWO, biological potential for the Progenitors, and the<br /> reliable coolness of high technology for Iteration X. As a whole,<br /> though, the Union concentrates upon keeping the Masses<br /> controlled, comforted, and dependent upon technology for\u2026<br /> well, everything. And in that regard, at least, they certainly<br /> do dominate the world.\u200b </div> </div> </div>This &quot;endless indulgence&quot; immediately makes me think of the Nephandic paradigm &quot;<i>Indulgence is Nature's Only Law</i>&quot;, a fact that it's not lost in Technocracy Reloaded, for the Syndicate's Paradigms (p.157): <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because such convictions often lead to corruption, certain<br /> Syndicate ops embrace the Sadean paradigm that Indulgence is<br /> Nature\u2019s Only Law, believe that I\u2019m a Predator and the World is<br /> My Prey, or \u2014 at its most solipsistic extreme \u2014 assert that I am<br /> All and therefore nothing else exists. These paradigms tend<br /> toward the Nephandic end of the belief spectrum, and so<br /> those holding them tend to be the most ruthless of their kind. </div> </div> </div>So... how can anyone redeem this in a new post-metaplot Technocracy? It seems to me that a new and benevolent Technocracy is a Technocracy without its Syndicate.<br /> <br /> (Credit where credit is due, &quot;fear of The Other&quot; is extremely Orwellian and not a good look to the NWO, but then again they are not THAT much better than the Syndicate)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-08T17:42:46-07:00","id":1559297,"title":"","content":"To me, it seems like the Syndicate may be the most redeemable of the lot. Their whole focus seems to be around capitalism and making money. Which is a far cry from creating genetically engineered super soldiers, turning people into killer cyborgs, trying to impose a fascist regime, or whatever else the other Conventions have gotten up to over the centuries. If you can convince them there is money to be made in pursuing a different course of action, they'd probably be on board.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the subject of redemption, bare in mind that causing a mage to question their paradigm royally fucks with their ability to use magic. In worst cases, it can even strip them of their magic completely. Paradigm is how you rationalize your ability to use magic, so anything that causes you to reexamine it is going to have dramatic effects on your entire world view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-08T20:56:52-07:00","id":1559298,"title":"","content":"While I understand this could get into areas not necessarily appropriate for a deep discussion here, I think the core question is something slightly different:<br /> <br /> Can capitalism be redeemed?<br /> <br /> As I see it, there's only two ways to redeemed the Syndicate. If you believe capitalism can be a force for good despite how things are currently going, then to a large extent the Syndicate just needs to get their heads out of their asses. Far too much of history, but especially since the rise of liberal democracy and secular humanism, has been dictated by people that are powerful through wealth putting short term gains over both long term self-interest as well as any sort of moral compass. The Syndicate, more than any other faction in the WoD, can be fairly asked, &quot;Why did you sit back and let all of this obviously prevented human suffering happen? Just to make the money line go up a bit this quarter?&quot; Especially in recent history, the global economy has seen disaster after disaster that somehow keeps ending up enriching the rich, and making the poor poorer. This is obviously in the Conventions worst interests because the masses are losing faith in the value of the markets. We have multiple generations that have moved farther and farther away from participating in the activities that the Syndicate can turn into Primal Ventures because they get at best an unlivable pittance out of it.<br /> <br /> The other option is to ditch capitalism for something else. Which as DarkKing noted is going to be very hard on the Syndicate because it involves a paradigm shift in multiple meanings of the word. If capitalism is irredeemable, than the only way to redeem the Syndicate is to have them be the forefront of a new economy that actually works for everyone. This means a lot of purging of the current membership for clinging to old ideas (not that this is new for the Union), and a wide-scale concerted effort by the reinvigorated Convention to take a much stronger hand in pushing the global system into one that encourages human flourishing without appealing to base desires, greed, and large scale social manipulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-08T22:06:03-07:00","id":1559299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559298#post1559298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The other option is to ditch capitalism for something else. Which as DarkKing noted is going to be very hard on the Syndicate because it involves a paradigm shift in multiple meanings of the word. If capitalism is irredeemable, than the only way to redeem the Syndicate is to have them be the forefront of a new economy that actually works for everyone. This means a lot of purging of the current membership for clinging to old ideas (not that this is new for the Union), and a wide-scale concerted effort by the reinvigorated Convention to take a much stronger hand in pushing the global system into one that encourages human flourishing without appealing to base desires, greed, and large scale social manipulation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Communism has never, ever worked in its entire history, and attempts to change to a digital currency seem to have been a scam the whole time. Not sure what kind of new economy the Syndicate could be at the forefront of, but it would take a hell of a lot of leverage to sway the public's viewpoint to accepting it.<br /> <br /> But yeah, that's something I find funny about the Technocracy. In their efforts to keep humanity safe, they made the world so gods damned boring that people are losing the motivation to try anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-08T22:25:31-07:00","id":1559300,"title":"","content":"I don't really want to get into a big thing about economic systems... but the Syndicate has economic magic as their whole thing. I might not be able to envision the ideal economy to replace capitalism, but I don't have magic powers or access to an education in hypereconomics.<br /> <br /> That said the whole, &quot;communism has never worked,&quot; line always bugs me because it acts like there's some example of communism being allowed to operate on its own terms to see if it can work thanks to the Cold War. From that sort of reductive perspective, capitalism has never really worked either. The only thing that has kept capitalism functional is layering Marxist social economics under capitalist structures into what most countries have: mixed economic systems. Even China, Laos, and Vietnam (the three nominally communist countries that are actually doing pretty well economically these days) have moved to a mixed-economy in their own ways.<br /> <br /> That said, I didn't promote a specific model in my post. If I meant communism I would have said so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-09T02:42:49-07:00","id":1559302,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the whole thread but if the Syndicate is to be reformed or redeemed then I think the idea of the &quot;Handelsgeist&quot; (the spirit of peaceful and mutually beneficial trade) would be the key. We're told that the groups the Syndicate grew out of wanted to replace war with trade and economic activity. The last Convention book for the Syndicate made it clear the Syndicate believes in productive use of time. It's clear that the Syndicate lost it's way when it changed trade replacing war for trade as the new form of war. Also switching from promotion of productive use of time to mandating that all time be dedicated to what they saw as productive use of time.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate needs to refocus on their original ideal of peace through mutually beneficial trade and promotion of productive use of time.<br /> <br /> A Native American community from California who called themselves &quot;the people who make shell money&quot; practiced something like the idea of the Handelsgeist. They made their money to replace war with trade. Maybe it would take Dreamspeakers to balance the Syndicate's books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-11-2026, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-09T06:07:00-07:00","id":1559303,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> really said the quiet part out loud, but yeah it's really a question of how capitalism can be redeemed (but that would necessitate another kind of discussion, one that I agree is not appropriate here).<br /> <br /> But moving away from such economic critiques and more into the realm of paradigms in-game, I think that the main issue on that front for not only the Syndicate but the entirety of the Technocratic Union is the pervasive presence of <i>Might is Right</i>. Of the five conventions, three of them in <i>Technocracy Reloaded </i>(NWO, Progenitors and the Syndicate) cite this paradigm as one that is present in these conventions (even though it seems to be a minor one for Progenitors compared to the NWO and Syndicate). And, sure, this is a paradigm, like any other, not exclusive to the Technocrats. It's present in the Order of Hermes, Society of Ether, Templar Knights, to name a few. Moreover, like any other paradigm it can be corrupted by the Nephandi, but to me is <i>especially</i> suscpetible to Nephandic corruption and exemplifies perfectly the excess of the Union. If <i>Might is Right</i>, then yes, NWO agent, you can use violent state repression to crush those Deviants; yes, Progenitor, you can start an outbreak just to see how the population survives; yes, Syndicate agent, you can exploit the weakness of the economy for your benefit, after all if <i>you can</i> <i>its in your right to do it</i>.<br /> <br /> Again, there's something to be said that this is not a Syndicate thing, but a Mage thing (<i>Might is Right</i> is quite a frequent paradigm), and how these temptations of power relates to the overaching theme of hubris in the game as a whole. But, <i>damn, </i>it seems to be a walk in the park to corrupt a Technocratic agent and a given if said agent is from the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> I think that a new Technocracy to really redeem itself needs to curb heavily this particular paradigm (they already do this type of thing for so many other &quot;deviant&quot; paradigms). But to specifically redeem the Syndicate, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a>. Trade and money are social technologies that allow people to communicate desires without the need for violence or out-right conflict, and I think that this argument can be made using the sphere of Primal Utility. Just like a Chorister uses Prime by fostering community in a religious institution, the Syndicate could view Primal Utility in the same manner of fostering prosperity for all, not just for the few.<br /> <br /> And still using another idea from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a>, I don't think that accumulating obscenes ammount of wealth in the hands of a few agents seems to promote a &quot;productive use of time&quot; in the Masses (or a productive use of time for the agent even, since he could grow quite complacent).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-09T06:08:19-07:00","id":1559304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559302#post1559302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the whole thread but if the Syndicate is to be reformed or redeemed then I think the idea of the &quot;Handelsgeist&quot; (the spirit of peaceful and mutually beneficial trade) would be the key. We're told that the groups the Syndicate grew out of wanted to replace war with trade and economic activity. The last Convention book for the Syndicate made it clear the Syndicate believes in productive use of time. It's clear that the Syndicate lost it's way when it changed trade replacing war for trade as the new form of war. Also switching from promotion of productive use of time to madating that all time be dedicated to what they saw as productive use of time.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate needs to refocus on their original ideal of peace through mutually beneficial trade and promotion of productive use of time.<br /> <br /> A Native American community from California who called themselves &quot;the people who make shell money&quot; practiced something like the idea of the Handelsgeist. They made their money to replace war with trade. Maybe it would take Dreamspeakers to balance the Syndicate's books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>&quot;People don't study kung fu to learn how to defeat their inner selves, or whatever. They do it because we made martial arts sexy&quot;</i> - Syndicate's opinion of the Akashic Brotherhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-09T09:07:34-07:00","id":1559306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559304#post1559304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;People don't study kung fu to learn how to defeat their inner selves, or whatever. They do it because we made martial arts sexy&quot;</i> - Syndicate's opinion of the Akashic Brotherhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would say that kind of view it's part of what makes the Syndicate evil - they understand real value comes from <i>people's activities</i> and not <i>money</i>, but they treat <i>people </i>(culture, values) as things to be marketed for proffit. They've avoided the &quot;trap of money&quot; to fall into a scheme where people and their values are little more than money - things to be exploited.<br /> <br /> They need to start seeing people as people, their activities as true value, rather than the sum of Primal Value they can <i>extract</i> to do the <i>other</i> stuff they want to do. <hr /><br /> They can't easily do this, tho. In a sense, the Syndicate it's victim to it's own success.<br /> <br /> They're the great providers of Quintessence for the Union, that allows it to make so many great works that improve the world - but because they can always use more juice, the Syndicate often ends employing extremely unethical methods to get more juice - from crime and war, to neglecting unscrupulous actors (like Pentex) to such a degree they end risking the end of the world.<br /> <br /> If they suddenly have to say NO (to the Union, and to themselves too) - As in: No, we're not going to risk the glacier's ecosystem to attract the kind of investments that work as our Quintessence batteries, because that will leave a worse future for everyone - then they loose power within the Union.<br /> <br /> If the Syndicate it's so populated by assholes, I would say that it's in part because that's exactly the kind of people that triumph on such an &quot;economy&quot; - so to speak. But if the rest of the Technocracy can get better, or wish to get better, I would say - so can the Syndicate. <hr /><br /> Why would they refuse this power?. Well, it's not going to be to make more money <i>for themselves</i>. You will always be able to make more juice for yourself (and even for the whole Union) if you turn people and the world into juice-making machines to be drained. Or increasing productivity, as they say.<br /> <br /> But they <i>could</i> if they cared about <i>the value of the world as a whole </i>- so to speak. Don't even need to stop being greedy for this. It's just a matter of changing a little perspective about what greed means, focusing on long term gains and sustainability. Realizing you're part of the whole, not above the whole, you start wanting &quot;the others&quot; to be better too<br /> <br /> -&gt;For instance: Let's say you plan to live a really long life. Then suddenly risking a natural catastrophe in the foreseable future isn't so smart, rigth?. But, of course, the Syndicate can believe they're going to survive somehow. Science it's going to solve it, if only for &quot;the elite&quot;. Because of course the rest of the Technocracy it's going to solve their fuck-ups - that's why they pay them.<br /> <br /> -&gt; This is the problem. The Syndicate believes themselves *above* the system, part of an elite that exists *above* the people that toil for them. IN part thanks to the Technocracy. But there's enough reason to believe this isn't going to always be the case: The world it's a dangerous place, you can't expect to create problems for others and *always* get away with it. That's how you end with a Pentex sending you the heads of your agents.<br /> <br /> If you're not *above* the whole, wouldn't it be <i>smarter</i> to care about it?<br /> <br /> A tentative Syndicate movement following this line of tougth (making a nod to the Akashicks example):<br /> <br /> &quot;<u>Cultivators of the World</u>&quot;<br /> *Trying to make a world where everyone has an easier time realizing their value it's the selling point and it's entirely in line with Primal Utility - humanity creates the value that defines the world.<br /> *The Paradigm however contemplates humanity as a network where every actor has the rigth to be empowered. Prioritizing long-term stability over short term wins, and the good of the many.<br /> *The core idea it's to strengthen <b>the value of the world</b>. The world being understood as that network that's co-dependant, if only a few links are empowered then the whole net it's weaker.<br /> *Often means blocking people from exploiting that value, on cases where that exploit it's hurting people's chances, or creating long term dangers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-09-2026, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-09T11:14:53-07:00","id":1559308,"title":"","content":"Overall, I tend to see the NWO as harder to redeem than the Syndicate, for the simple reason the Syndicate views people as an opportunity and the NWO sees people as an obstacle. That means that even though both Conventions are terrible about stripping away human dignity and treating the masses as exploitable objects, the Syndicate has a better philosophical foundation to improve. It's not where they are now, but they at least have a foundation that can (potentially) see the inherent value in the human person and in human dignity. <br /> <br /> To put it another way, the Syndicate falls into the trap of viewing people as statistics, but when they actually meet individual people there's real potential for them to see value and possibility and mutually beneficial options. Meanwhile the NWO more often falls into the trap of viewing humanity as an ideal, so when they meet individual people there's more potential for them to see disappointment and conflict and expendability.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-09T12:38:45-07:00","id":1559310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559308#post1559308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall, I tend to see the NWO as harder to redeem than the Syndicate, for the simple reason the Syndicate views people as an opportunity and the NWO sees people as an obstacle. That means that even though both Conventions are terrible about stripping away human dignity and treating the masses as exploitable objects, the Syndicate has a better philosophical foundation to improve. It's not where they are now, but they at least have a foundation that can (potentially) see the inherent value in the human person and in human dignity.<br /> <br /> To put it another way, the Syndicate falls into the trap of viewing people as statistics, but when they actually meet individual people there's real potential for them to see value and possibility and mutually beneficial options. Meanwhile the NWO more often falls into the trap of viewing humanity as an ideal, so when they meet individual people there's more potential for them to see disappointment and conflict and expendability.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the NWO was fully on board with the Nazi regime.<br /> <br /> Their long term goal is to impose a singular world government, a singular culture or nation. No deviation or clashing of ideals, but everybody submitting themselves to the same rational paradigm under their control.<br /> <br /> One convention has a compulsive spending problem, while the other thinks colonialism and global genocide are ultimately good for humanity as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-09T14:45:06-07:00","id":1559312,"title":"","content":"I don't want to give the Syndicate a free pass, they have bigger problems than compulsive spending. Reducing people to numbers on a page and cogs in a machine is seriously dehumanizing and I have no interest in sugar coating that so that they compare better to the NWO.<br /> <br /> But of the two, I can much more easily see the NWO deliberately committing atrocities. The Syndicate is more likely to realize that its view of people doesn't match the people and reconsider its actions (if only for better results). The NWO is more likely to see that its view of people doesn't match the people and decide that it's <i>the people</i> who need to be replaced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-09T15:34:22-07:00","id":1559314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559310#post1559310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the NWO was fully on board with the Nazi regime.<br /> <br /> Their long term goal is to impose a singular world government, a singular culture or nation. No deviation or clashing of ideals, but everybody submitting themselves to the same rational paradigm under their control.<br /> <br /> One convention has a compulsive spending problem, while the other thinks colonialism and global genocide are ultimately good for humanity as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh... to summarize the problem with the Syndicate as &quot;compulsive spending&quot; astronomically diminshes the extent of the corruption of the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> First of all, a sizeable chunk of the Syndicate operations deal with the criminal underworld. Sure, contraband of some illicit goods could be harmless enough and just wind up in the compulsive spending type of situation, but a good portion of organized crime deals with human trafficking, a topic extensively discussed in <i>The Book of The Fallen. </i>In this case, it stops being a issue of mere indulgence and harkens back to the philosophical issue of seeing people as objects to extract value from.<br /> <br /> Second, colonialism is a project that the Syndicate endorses as much as the NWO. One of the first financial markets that would model our current system of stock exchange was the Amsterdam Stock Exchange, that would finance much of the colonial projects of the Netherlands in Asia. The main impulse in a lot of colonial endeavors was to siphon natural resources and labor (a lot of the time, slave labor) from the colonies to the mainland. All of this is <i>crucial </i>to the development of capitalism in what today constitutes developed countries.<br /> <br /> Third, I know that in Revised the metaplot converges to an enforcing of the Pogrom, resulting in the genocide of the Crafts. But this is a Technocratic Union at large action, not an specific NWO venture. I tend to agree with Brucato in M20 that this, even if made sense that Technocracy would do such a thing, I don't believe is a good idea because it <i>completly</i> undermines any chance of nuance in its portrayal, even if you believe that the Technocracy is hopelessly corrupt. Per <i>The Book of Secrets</i>, p. 262:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First off, as bad as the Technocracy could be, the idea<br /> that they suddenly decided to go on a global killing spree \u2013<br /> exterminating hundreds, probably thousands, of human beings<br /> while wiping a bunch of cultural small-t traditions off the map<br /> within a matter of weeks \u2013 seemed extreme even by 1990s<br /> standards. </div> </div> </div>So, yeah, even though the idea of massive genocide would be present in the NWO or any convention, I don't believe it would be something endorsed in the Technocracy as a whole, at least not in a Technocracy capable of redemption or how the faction evolves throughout the M20 books.<br /> <br /> Then, the issue with the NWO and the Axis powers. In many parts of WoD, the writers tend to avoid explicit casuality between the splats, be it vampire or mage, and the ascension of the Nazis (correctly so, considering that it's one of the most, if not the most horrific period of human history). But, again, focusing only on Mage, this is not a problem with just the NWO, but with the entire Technocracy (Hell, Mengele might be the go-to Progenitor villain if a campaign takes place in this period). Not just the Technocracy mind you, but even some sections of the Traditions would be involved in this undertaking, given that a core influence in nazi ideology was esoteric thinking such as those of Julius Evola. And, again, it's implied that both the Traditions and the Technocracy at some point joined forces to fight the nazis and the Nephandi that were in their midst. In fact, this notion of Tradition, Disparate and Technocracy rallying together to fight the Nephandi is proposed for the current metaplot scenario in M20, per <i>M20 Corebook</i> p.135:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Technocracy\u2019s victory party was premature</b>: Sure, the Union got the upper hand, but the Traditions and<br /> Disparates have survived worse. Hubris leads most Technocrats to consider the fight more or less over\u2026 and to<br /> miss the Nephandic leadership now governing their every move. The Masses surprise everyone with their<br /> combination of self-indulgence, fanaticism, and hope for a better tomorrow. The Traditions rally once again, and the Disparates<br /> band together to take back their world. Loyal Technocrats who\u2019ve discovered the Inner Circle\u2019s corruption stage a<br /> shadow-war within the Union, possibly allying with Tradition and Disparate sects in an effort to rescue the ideals of<br /> science from Nephandic infiltration. At the moment, though, the Fallen are winning what\u2019s left of the Ascension<br /> War. It\u2019s like WWII all over again, with even higher stakes\u200b </div> </div> </div>Besides, going back to<i> Guide to The Technocracy</i>, this historical error is something that Technocrats are aware and trying to prevent, per p.75:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the Union's deepest shames is its early support of Nazi Germany. Many Technocrats<br /> - especially the architects of Project Invictus - are watching to make sure nothing like that<br /> happens again. </div> </div> </div>Nevertheless, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>. By singling out the Syndicate, I ended up being way too charitable to the NWO. Still, I personally believe that institutional order (without the fascism) is a more easy to imagine redemptive goal than overhauling economic institutions and paradigms. One example of a current issue which a see an NWO agent struggling but still capable of resolving is the problem with rampant desinformation, one which The Feed could tackle. There is a fine line between ensuring that desinformation is not produced and not curbing the free speech of people, but still I find this conflict is more approachable than a Syndicate agent going against the corporate maxim of pursuing profit to tend to the common good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-09T15:39:09-07:00","id":1559315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559312#post1559312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to give the Syndicate a free pass, they have bigger problems than compulsive spending. Reducing people to numbers on a page and cogs in a machine is seriously dehumanizing and I have no interest in sugar coating that so that they compare better to the NWO.<br /> <br /> But of the two, I can much more easily see the NWO deliberately committing atrocities. The Syndicate is more likely to realize that its view of people doesn't match the people and reconsider its actions (if only for better results). The NWO is more likely to see that its view of people doesn't match the people and decide that it's <i>the people</i> who need to be replaced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quality over quantity; people are much more willing to keep giving you money, if they're satisfied with what you're selling them.<br /> <br /> Again, if you can convince the Syndicate that there's money to be made in pursuing a different course of action, they'd probably be willing to at least give it some consideration.<br /> <br /> It's not like they've gone full blown Mammonite, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-09T21:41:40-07:00","id":1559317,"title":"","content":"I mean, I'm a pinko commie who despises Capitalism, and think the very system exists to recapitulate the systems and power structures of Feudalism in a post-Guillotine world. And, given how much that system has both hyper-fucked humanity AND poisoned the well on alternatives to it for over a hundred years...I have <i>zero patience</i> to treat it as an equally valid belief system. Call a Neo-Liberal Centrist if you want someone who entertains a contrary position to that out of...&quot;good sportsmanship&quot;, I guess.<br /> <br /> Every day, I get to watch Capitalism kill the planet and push for genocidal invasions over oil. I have no interest in playing fair.<br /> <br /> Would it be possible to rehabilitate the Syndicate? Personally, I don't think I'd WANT to. They are, to me, the designated Villain convention in the Technocratic Union, even if individual members might be morally nuanced and interesting. Their utility, to ME, is as antagonists, and as the Token Evil Teammate in Technocracy games that bankroll the whole operation.<br /> <br /> If Capitalism collapsed (*fingers crossed*), and that effectively destroyed the Syndicate...well, sucks to suck. <i>Let them die</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-09T22:27:29-07:00","id":1559318,"title":"","content":"I am frankly bewildered that out of the towering mountain of evils and fuck ups the Technocracy has been responsible for over the centuries, it is their ruthless capitalism that's causing us to have the redemption arc debate.<br /> <br /> Let's not forget about the fact the friggin BORG are on their way to earth as we speak, and the Void Engineers have refused to share that knowledge with the rest of the class.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T01:12:13-07:00","id":1559321,"title":"","content":"In the Void Engineer's book a key difference between the Syndicate and the NWO was mentality. The NWO assumes that you righteously ought to obey them. They demand your conformity. The Syndicate wants to buy you. The Syndicate needs to try to understand others even if it is for totally selfish reasons. The NWO needs to make others comform, by force if need be, which is brutal even if the reasons are totally selfless and virtuous.<br /> <br /> Even the most monterously corrupt Syndicate member has some reason to be aware of the other person's worldview. It's not basically different from a wolf's need to understand its prey, but any awareness is a start.<br /> <br /> Both organizations are evil but the NWO wants to force you to obey and the Syndicate prefers seduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T03:37:56-07:00","id":1559322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559318#post1559318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am frankly bewildered that out of the towering mountain of evils and fuck ups the Technocracy has been responsible for over the centuries, it is their ruthless capitalism that's causing us to have the redemption arc debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately because there's a core issue with the Syndicate that prompted this thread in the first place. All of the Conventions are fucked up and evil in their ways because the Technocracy was explicitly evil faction until the very end of 2e when there was a move to make them more nuanced; which continued into Revised and M20. But for the most part the Convention have easily identifiable core appeals at the center of their rotten structures. For ItX, the Progenitors, and even the VEs, the path towards redemption is simple to <b>envision</b> regardless of how hard it might be in the current state of the setting (keeping in mind that the OP noted one of the less evil takes on the M20 version of the setting). They need to have their members working more on what's better for humanity instead of what crazy as shit they want to poke, or create to poke in a lab. The NWO is a bit more complicated because their expertise in social sciences has always been a tool not a primary academic focus on the Convention. But that said, large scale human societies need people running the system. We need people making decisions in the background that are both really important (and thus really easy to abuse) just the rest of us can do whatever we're doing with our lives. Even the best journalists and news sources curate what you will learn from them because there's simply too much news in the world to digest it all. Without someone making the editorial decisions of what news to print, the rest of society knows nothing.<br /> <br /> This is where the Syndicate becomes an outlier. They're the only Convention built exclusively around promoting and maintaining a specific system within human society. Everything wrong with them in inescapably tied to capitalism. They're not the economist Convention, they're the private equity firm Convention. Anyone in this thread could easily rattle off a list of things ItX should be doing instead of making killer cyborgs to murder RDs, but it's a change in priorities instead of a change in how they would actually operate in terms of advancing research and technology in the public sphere. If the Syndicate was forced to abandon capitalism... what would they even be exactly?<br /> <br /> I also think you might be hung up on the word &quot;redemption.&quot; You're talking about redemption in terms of making up for past wrongs, where the main point of the OP is more redeeming the institutions into forces of good in the world. The question is not, &quot;how do the Void Engineers make good on screwing up with Threat Null,&quot; but what would a future version of them look like where these sorts of problems aren't ones they help cause in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T04:39:57-07:00","id":1559324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559322#post1559322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think you might be hung up on the word &quot;redemption.&quot; You're talking about redemption in terms of making up for past wrongs, where the main point of the OP is more redeeming the institutions into forces of good in the world. The question is not, &quot;how do the Void Engineers make good on screwing up with Threat Null,&quot; but what would a future version of them look like where these sorts of problems aren't ones they help cause in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This. The question is not, &quot;What could [Convention] do to make up for its crimes?&quot;<br /> <br /> The question is, &quot;What does a hypothetical GOOD version of [Convention] look like?&quot;<br /> <br /> Without, of course, fundamentally changing what that Convention is about. (Like, someone might insist that the best version of the Progenitors is one that rejects pharmeceuticals and embraces spirit healing; but they wouldn't really be the Progenitors, now would they?).<br /> <br /> The Syndicate sticks out because its faults - the &quot;why it's Evil&quot; - is tied fundamentally to the faults and evils of the Capitalist system. (Because Capitalism exists to consolidate wealth into the hands of increasingly fewer people, and rig every aspect of the systems around it to support infinite growth in that direction). You cannot make a hypothetical &quot;Good&quot; version of the Syndicate, without them ceasing to be Capitalist. Without them becoming something unrecognizable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T08:13:38-07:00","id":1559327,"title":"","content":"I think the Friends of Courage and Project Invictus could pave a way &quot;redeemption&quot; for the NWO. Yeah. they're multi-convention, but they're strongly influenced by the NWO and both seem forces for good.<br /> <br /> *The Friends of Courage are secret agents that do concentrate on rigthing wrongs rather than just blindly following the party line. I had the imporession they were popular among NWO agents (that Courage was part of), proving that there <i>are</i> those that aren't <i>all</i> about blindly following the party line<br /> <br /> *Invictus plays more on the idea of the need of an overseer group that controls things, on the other hand, but focused more on figthing corruption.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, NWO flaws mirror those of the Syndicate as they <i>too </i>believe to be &quot;above the masses&quot;, but in a different sense. NWO has a problem with the &quot;individual&quot; more than with &quot;people on general&quot;. They don't have much roblem with understanding and molding to peoples values - they have gender equality and other progressive factions after all. But they have no place to see people as &quot;individuals&quot;. They <i>mold </i>the individual to conform the group (Room 101). They need to see people as humans with rigths rather than as a<i> general consensus</i><br /> <br /> But it really doesn't matter if they're disapointed on individuals as long as they don't see themselves as <i>so above</i> <i>the rest as to just trample over them</i> <i>completely</i>. Maybe that's not going to make them perfectly aligned with democratic values, but if a FoC were to gain enough prominency to close Room 101 - that alone would be a <i>huge </i>step foward. And, even if that makes the Union a bit more prone to defection I think people it's going to be mostly OK with this. <hr /><br /> One of the problems of the Syndicate it's that they <i>don't</i> have a group opposed to their issues, AFAIK.<br /> <br /> We know there are individuals at least <i>trying:</i> It's said that some Syndics <i>try </i>to do Socialism for all the right reasons - they <i>fail</i>, but even then that must mean <i>some </i><i>see </i><i>there are issues, </i>rigth<i>?</i>. However they lack any kind of support or cohesion about these efforts. And these individuals lack of success sort of forces them back to the fold and <i>conform </i>to what they clearly see as evil (or become Etherites, as we can see in the SoE Trad Book)<br /> <br /> And then there's neo-SPD, that's a joke: The Syndicate it's responsible of one of the worst fuck-ups of the Technocracy on Pentex, and yet their answer to this it's to<i> figth</i><i>everyone else that's trying to stop SPD </i>(for good reasons, maybe? As it could mean the balance of power between them and the NWO breaks, dooming the Union - but even if we believe that, it's just another case of them being prisioners of their own success)<br /> <br /> I think there's merit to try and make a Syndicate branch that isn't all about protecting the Status Quo, since that could serve as a clutch or plot-hook to actually figth the Syndicate's problems from within.<br /> <br /> It would help if they were less obsessed with &quot;increasing wealth&quot;, and finding human value on things that don't make lots of money on the short run, but are important for long term wellfare. Such as Human Rigths institutions as something that protects humanity intrinsic value. Public or semi-private health institutions increasing living standards. Or the inherent value of an ecosystem as the structure that makes life possible. NWO being able to to use PU to extract value from public institutions shows that diversifying the concept it's, at least, <i>contemplated</i>. Even if not by the Syndics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":".  I misnamed the Friends of Courage :P 04-10-2026, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T09:11:50-07:00","id":1559329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559322#post1559322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The NWO is a bit more complicated because their expertise in social sciences has always been a tool not a primary academic focus on the Convention. But that said, large scale human societies need people running the system. We need people making decisions in the background that are both really important (and thus really easy to abuse) just the rest of us can do whatever we're doing with our lives. Even the best journalists and news sources curate what you will learn from them because there's simply too much news in the world to digest it all. Without someone making the editorial decisions of what news to print, the rest of society knows nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I find the NWO more easy to imagine in an redeemed state. One of the most common Extraordinary Citizens I imagine the NWO have is the kind of banal city burocrat, that although seems to have an useless desk job, is an essential piece of how a city function. An agent of the NWO most of the time could be one of those infamous Black Suits that raze a chantry to the ground, but could also easily be one government employee with the mission of guaranteeing that elections run smoothly. Even that Black Suit in a new NWO could have a new purpose, instead of rounding up deviant mages who would not be in a any way a real threat to humanity at large, and instead focus their might in curbing arms trade in order to guarantee stability (something that I guarantee would displease the Syndicate). That's how I see a way to redeem the NWO, move on from &quot;fear of The Other&quot; to focus on the core technocrat mission of &quot;control&quot; and &quot;stability&quot;. To tackle its own hubris, the NWO needs to (like ItX) accept (or at least tolerate) a certain degree of difference with its own models of Humanity and refocus on guaranteeing the stability needed for the Masses to thrive.<br /> <br /> Although the Syndicate can see the individual and this would open a avenue for reforming their convention, in the end their paradigms and philosphies utterly commodify human experience. Sure, each convention could be accused of that, ItX seeing people as machine and Progenitors seeing people as just lumps of flesh to be molded as the Scientist dictates, but these points of view don't seem to be how these Conventions at large work in a post-Dimensional Anamoly setting. But the endgame of the Syndicate, even to those more idealist in the spectrum, is the commodification of Reality.<br /> <br /> Two paragraphs from <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i> dedicated to the Syndicate illustrate this point (p.152):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Love? True friendship? Hope? Salvation? People like to say<br /> that such things can\u2019t be bought; when you come right down to<br /> it, though, they can \u2014 because everything can be bought \u2014 and<br /> whatever can be bought can, by definition, be sold. Across the<br /> length and breadth of the universe, there\u2019s nothing that can\u2019t<br /> ultimately be commodified. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It all comes together to form the essence of the Bottom<br /> Line, the driving ethos of the Syndicate: everything is for sale,<br /> one way or another. We\u2019re all just haggling over price.\u200b </div> </div> </div>The problem with the Syndicate is not that they are just rich and indulgent, since there are rich mages that are not in the Syndicate. The Wu Lung, Solificati (both of which have a core mystic tradition around gold and its transcendetal aspects), House Fortunae of the Hermetics, all of these factions have core practices that can make the Mage really rich, but their worldview around riches is alien to the Syndicate. For each of them, material wealth is just a consequence of their Arts or a reflection of inner transcendence, while for the Syndicate the accumulation of wealth is not just a consequence, it constitutes their paradigms, their practices, <i>the core identity of the Syndicate is Capital.</i><br /> <br /> Which comes around to the very question <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Arms proposed in the beginning and again on the above post. For the Syndicate to be redeemed we have to question whether the system in which they fundament their practices is redeemable. If it is, then the Syndicate can be rehabilitated and be part of this Neo-Technocracy as it renews a vision of sheparding the Masses with desire and commerce, not just themselves. If it is not, the fundamental changes that it would necessitate for a change in their Convention are so vast that whatever comes out the other side is not the Syndicate anymore, but an entire new Convention.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T10:38:32-07:00","id":1559330,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> There are two things that commonly get muddled in comparisons of the Syndicate and the NWO. For the Syndicate, they run afoul common disconnect present in most casual discussions of economics: because people often use the same terms differently. Some people use the term capitalism in a very general sense to mean any economic system with people trading based on wants and needs. Others use it to refer to very specific applications of it, commonly the ones we see in the modern west right now. The more specifically we define capitalism it and the more we tie the Syndicate to the specific modern economic system, the more difficult it is to change them without it seeming like a dramatic break. On the flip side, if they are tied to capitalist systems in general and able to switch away from the current one, they can change quite a bit while still being the same Convention.<br /> <br /> That isn't an argument for which of those ways they should be depicted, by the way, just a statement of the options and how they relate to Syndicate reform.<br /> <br /> For the NWO, the problem is the discussion tends to revolve around whether state regulation and control can be a force for good (itself a quite controversial topic) but misses that the NWO is not a state. They aren't elected, they have no Mandate of Heaven, no divine right of kings, they didn't get a sword from some watery tart, they don't have the right of conquest, and most importantly, they don't assert themselves as a government or an arm of a government. They are a shadowy conspiracy that has appointed itself to secretly manipulate the people whether they like it or not. A lot of mage groups (especially the Conventions) have that issue to one extent or another, but the NWO have it to a profound degree and character. They aren't the halls of power, they are the corruption in the halls of power: unknown and unaccountable. Redeeming that is considerably harder than just shifting their motivations. It requires major changes in justification and accountability.<br /> <br /> Note, this is not an argument that the NWO are morally worse than the Syndicate, it is pointing out a specific Achilles' heel they have that makes reformation very difficult without changing their very nature. It is a problem most of the Conventions have, but one that is much more significant for the NWO because of their focus and how they relate to it.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Also, as a side note: I tend to get a lot of pushback on this, but it's been my headcanon that the Syndicate is the Convention of economic systems, not just capitalist ones. Indeed, if they are tied to the value of human endeavor rather than money itself, it makes sense that they would be. I think they've done a at least some experimenting around with planned and communist economies and they may do so again in the future. But as I said, that's mostly headcanon, so feel free to disregard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T12:05:15-07:00","id":1559331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559330#post1559330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the NWO, the problem is the discussion tends to revolve around whether state regulation and control can be a force for good (itself a quite controversial topic) but misses that the NWO is not a state. They aren't elected, they have no Mandate of Heaven, no divine right of kings, they didn't get a sword from some watery tart, they don't have the right of conquest, and most importantly, they don't assert themselves as a government or an arm of a government. <b>They are a shadowy conspiracy that has appointed itself to secretly manipulate the people whether they like it or not. </b>A lot of mage groups (especially the Conventions) have that issue to one extent or another, but the NWO have it to a profound degree and character. They aren't the halls of power, they are the corruption in the halls of power: unknown and unaccountable. Redeeming that is considerably harder than just shifting their motivations. It requires major changes in justification and accountability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've just described the Technocracy itself. The Syndicate included.<br /> <br /> NWO has this as a profound degree and character because, as their book says (and it's true), they're the &quot;soul&quot; of the Technocracy. Their ideologues and guides, and the &quot;brain&quot;.<br /> <br /> Maybe <i>the Technocracy </i>it's hard to redeem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T14:19:22-07:00","id":1559333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559330#post1559330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the NWO, the problem is the discussion tends to revolve around whether state regulation and control can be a force for good (itself a quite controversial topic) but misses that the NWO is not a state. </div> </div> </div> </div>Hm... this line of reasoning really elucidates that personal bias I talked about in my first post. I tend to be more amenable to the idea that state regulation can be a force for good, than the current economy system (capitalism) being a force for good, even though there's plenty of evidence that not being the case in a multitude of situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559330#post1559330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as a side note: I tend to get a lot of pushback on this, but it's been my headcanon that the Syndicate is the Convention of economic systems, not just capitalist ones. Indeed, if they are tied to the value of human endeavor rather than money itself, it makes sense that they would be. I think they've done a at least some experimenting around with planned and communist economies and they may do so again in the future. But as I said, that's mostly headcanon, so feel free to disregard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe that's entirely unreasonable. If each Convention is reduced to its core phrase of &quot;Enlightment through X&quot; (Ex.: ItX - Enlightment Through Precision and Quantifiable Perfection), than the Syndicate's line of &quot;Enlightment Through Commerce, Desire, and Exchange&quot; is within your concept. The thing is that what you called our modern economic system is too ubiquitous, with the alternatives being constantly sidelined (which would make sense in-game if the Syndicate agents that would opt for other economic systems that aren't capitalism, or at least our current mode of capitalism, being constantly put down by the rest of the Convention). And, to give more credence to your idea, in the post that I mentioned in the beginning &quot;(Heroic (or at least decent) Syndicate characters?&quot;) it was discussed how markets are not something exclusively tied to a capitalist economic system (how much that is true or not, I didn't verify).<br /> <hr /><br /> Now for the case of how difficult it is to redeem the Technocracy, I think that is the case, yeah. As I said, I chose from 3 distinct metaplot options, and the one I chose was the most charitable to redemption. The first assumes that the Union is hopeless and impossible to save and the other assumes that it's not metaphysically corrupt... even though it is undeniably ruthless. Still, they are my favorite faction and I like the idea of at least the <i>possibility </i>of redemption for them. In some of my previous posts, I questioned whether a Technocrat could achieve Ascension (the Personal kind), and now this thread deals a little with the other side of those questions, whether the Uplift Ideal is even possible with the extent of corruption in the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I like the idea of all the works from 2E to M20 culminating in a reckoning for the Technocracy. This Neo-Technocracy (as I called earlier, but the name is a work in progress) could be so radically different that it's propable in that kind of scenario there isn't even something like the Ascension War, since a substantially more benevolent and human Technocracy wouldn't be the same one that wages war against the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T15:46:08-07:00","id":1559334,"title":"","content":"While I don't want to get too side tracked, the thing about arguments against &quot;state regulation&quot; are generally against the modern concept of a &quot;state&quot; far more than they are about the need for regulations (even really hardcore anti-regulation advocates don't mean no regulations, they just want less rules for the stuff they want to do). Humans need social rules once a group gets big enough. You can't get a thousand people to live cooperatively and in a mutually beneficial fashion without enforceable explicated rules. We're just not wired for it. To that end, when it comes at least to internal matters, regulation is the whole purpose of the state. <br /> <br /> Much like my point before about the relationship between the Syndicate and capitalism, &quot;regulation&quot; is a necessary component of any system of human governance. Anti-statist models change who makes the regulations and/or who enforces them; even if they want to call the societal rules that govern internal behaviors something different. The Neo-NWO needs to drop the emphasis on controlling the rules-making apparatus of society, and shift to pushing it to work as best as possible under its own terms. It doesn't really matter if whatever method humans use to organize themselves is the modern state concept or something else. Either there's a method to make and force rules on the people because it's necessary for groups of a large enough size to even function and thus there's something for the NWO to work with, or humanity has splintered into such small social units that most of the Technocracy loses its central purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T21:13:20-07:00","id":1559337,"title":"","content":"While I hate the Technocracy and the world they're trying to create, I would reluctantly accept the compromise of allowing the <b>Etherites</b> or the <b>Virtual Adepts</b> to win the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> It would still be a world ruled by technomancy, but at least it would be more fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T21:20:29-07:00","id":1559338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559337#post1559337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I hate the Technocracy and the world they're trying to create, I would reluctantly accept the compromise of allowing the <b>Etherites</b> or the <b>Virtual Adepts</b> to win the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> It would still be a world ruled by technomancy, but at least it would be more fun!</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would anyone spend all that time, money and energy towards mapping out the human genome, and then NOT use it to recreate the Isle of Doctor Moreau?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T01:30:14-07:00","id":1559341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559337#post1559337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I hate the Technocracy and the world they're trying to create, I would reluctantly accept the compromise of allowing the <b>Etherites</b> or the <b>Virtual Adepts</b> to win the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> It would still be a world ruled by technomancy, but at least it would be more fun!</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. The VAs kinda <i>did</i> win in RL. Like, the ideas and movements that the VAs are a riff on are both hugely influential and powerful in the present. The difference comes from the books wanting the VAs to remain cool cyberpunks, rather than the kinds of people who want to talk about race IQ stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T01:56:32-07:00","id":1559342,"title":"","content":"So, I'm going to question what corruption is and what redemption means. I'm also going to question whether Mage organizations, Technocracy or other, are personalities or offered frameworks for human existence. <br /> Viewing the factions as personalities is the easiest conception to hold in our minds.<i>They </i>are <i>this</i> and <i>those</i> <i>others</i> are that. Then we can generalize behaviors and actions as a whole and judge them according to whatever criteria we see fit.<br /> Viewing the factions as frameworks, however, gets more complicated in the mind. If the Syndicate and others are defined by their models or paradigms, then they are offering a sandbox for everyone to play in. That means, while the Technocracy is certainly making the rules for a lot of things, they are neither the only players nor the only shapers of their own systems and their implementations.<br /> The text regularly conflates these two visions, often by design to muddy the eaters and also to allow variations of play. Each table has to make decisions, either conciously or unconsciously, about how much mages, and by extension, the Technocracy, control reality and how much they are just pushing ideas out as possibilities and trying to keep up with the myriad of variations Sleepers, or the Masses, turn those into.<br /> Every opportunity creates a potential, even a need, for corruption. Once others are allowed to work with your udeas they are going to change and reinterpret your ideas. Where this is corruption where it is growth and where it is evolution are actually quite subjective, up to a point.<br /> So, consider the corner shop keeper of whatever type you like. The opportunity to own and run a shop is an opening of the pattern to allow growth. Nice. However, when that same shopkeeper runs into financial trouble from mismanagement or outside pressures or environmental shifts (deportation, gentrification, general economic depression, whatever) there are some desperate choices to be made. Do they close the shop? Sell at a loss? Or maybe start allowing drugs to run through their shop or gambling or launder money for others to keep things going?<br /> The latter choices are obviously corruption. Is that the Syndicate causing that? The Nephandi? Some Tradition or Craft mages? Or is it the shop keeper's choice to go simpler routes rather than foresee events and make more positive changes? Is this because the Syndicate system is evil or just a lack of predictive soothsayers who could have read the stars fir rhem to help them out? Should we need to consult astrologers to run a business or us it better to be enabled with the self determinism to fail or succeed by our own choices?<br /> So the creation of opportunities, which is a big part of the Syndicate model, is also the opening to failure, hardship and corruption. Is the Syndicate corrupt for promoting this model, or just imperfect? Are they dominating these choices at the micro level or painting with broad strokes and trying to keep up with the consequences?<br /> How each of us thinks about this at our tables will create the &quot;objective&quot; truths about how good or bad each faction is and how much we care, based on each faction's impact to our characters and their passions and interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12269-heilong","name":"Heilong","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T03:11:59-07:00","id":1559343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559338#post1559338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would anyone spend all that time, money and energy towards mapping out the human genome, and then NOT use it to recreate the Isle of Doctor Moreau?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they read the book, realized the Doctor Moreau was a satirical critique of God in Genesis and decided medical research was less cruel and more rewarding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T03:25:11-07:00","id":1559344,"title":"","content":"The true key to the flaws of the Technocracy was summed up by William Blake &quot;May God bless and you keep/from single vision and Newton's sleep.&quot; The Technocracy is the most powerful group of Mages stuck in the &quot;my way or the highway&quot; mentality. And when someone takes that attitude towards you the highway always looks good. <br /> <br /> The Technocracy sees itself as holding the one true answer, the <b>Void Engineers</b> aren't nearly as narrow minded as the other four so they seem the most human. If the other convenions perceived the benefits of multiple viewpoints they could reach out to the Traditions and find ways to promote a better more sane world. <br /> <br /> If that happened, the Disparates would step up and be the villains. After all, about half of those organizations are as close minded as the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T03:37:04-07:00","id":1559345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heilong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559342#post1559342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Viewing the factions as frameworks, however, gets more complicated in the mind. If the Syndicate and others are defined by their models or paradigms, then they are offering a sandbox for everyone to play in. That means, while the Technocracy is certainly making the rules for a lot of things, they are neither the only players nor the only shapers of their own systems and their implementations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The catch is that the Technocracy are keeping all the best toys to themselves and not letting anybody else play with them.<br /> <br /> The masses don't get the super drug that makes you immortal. The masses don't get plasma cannons, or FTL starships, or memory wiping flash sticks. The masses don't get to explore distant planets, until the Technocracy lands there first and sanitizes everything.<br /> <br /> The masses don't get any of the 'hyper science' goodies the Technocracy has up their sleeves. Allegedly under the pretense of Consensus not being able to accept their existence at the moment.<br /> <br /> But that consensus is rooted in Technocratic dogma, so the mere fact that this technology can exist at all means that they've already figured out a way to rationalize it.<br /> <br /> Have you seen those computers with the liquid tubes inside of them? When I saw a picture of one for the first time, I literally asked if the computer was powered by alchemy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 04-11-2026, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T07:04:00-07:00","id":1559349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559344#post1559344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that happened, the Disparates would step up and be the villains. After all, about half of those organizations are as close minded as the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe the Disparates are villain material. The Disparate Alliance in M20 was formed with the notion of survival, specifically to defend themselves and their communities against the Technocratic Pogrom, which in turn they believe to be corrupted by the Nephandi. They are close-minded, sure, but I don't believe they would want to vie for the reformating of Reality (although I cannot argument in favor for the Solificati, Wu Lung or Ahl-i-Batin on that front because of these groups notions of Global Ascension). They are written as the &quot;collateral damage&quot; of the Ascension War anyway, it wouldn't make sense for them to continue the very war that shattered their cultures. And their close-mindness is different from technocratic dogma, it sprouts from a place of guarding their communities (and their Reality Zones) from the encroaching of Technocratic Consensus, while the close-mindness of The Technocracy comes from a place of subjugating Reality in order to establish one and irrefutable Consensus, ignoring the diversity inherent to the very Reality they want to protect. The formation of the Alliance could very well make these groups more acceptable of each other's differences, just like it happened to the Traditions in the course of their history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T07:52:43-07:00","id":1559350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559345#post1559345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The masses don't get any of the 'hyper science' goodies the Technocracy has up their sleeves. Allegedly under the pretense of Consensus not being able to accept their existence at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how you define the state of Consensus in your game. In M20, 3 scenarios are proposed for the ST: 1) <b>The Technocracy Won: </b>the pervasive belief in technology subjugate any mystical paradigm and it would be something like you said, which would really cast doubt in the Technocracy's good intentions in not giving their hypertech to the Masses; 2) <b>Technocratic Belief Dominates Certain Parts of the World</b>: this one punch holes in the notion of a Technocratic Consensus and the existence of Reality Zones would make the Technocracy be more careful with when, where, and how to introduce hypertech in regions of the world where it would generate Paradox/Rejection/Correction; 3) <b>Reality's in Flux: </b>this scenario laughs at the idea of any Consensus, giving the opportunity to make vulgar magick into coincidental magick and the opposite for ceratin kinds of technology. <hr /><br /> Another thing I don't think is accurate is to frame the conflict between the Traditions (or any mystic Mage) and the Technocracy as an issue of the existence of technology. Since <i>Guide to The Traditions</i>, technology is said to be present in the ranks of the Council, even beyond the halls of the Society of Ether and the Virtual Adepts. The presence of technology in the Traditions is even more pervasive by the time of M20 in <i>Lore of The Traditions</i>, even being a major source of inner conflict in some groups like the Verbena. The distinction between the Traditions and Technocracy is not one of &quot;Technology Bad vs Technology Good&quot; (if it was sure, let the VAs and Etherites have at it), but of what paradigms are <i>allowed</i> to exist and which ones should shape Consensus. The Technocracy is not merely the party of technology, but the party of Order, Stability and above all <i>Control</i>. The Science of the SoE and VAs is rooted in technology/technomagick, but is utterly anathema to the Technocracy because is not &quot;ordely&quot;, stable and thus it cannot be properly controlled. The need for sanitization before any introduction of technocratic hypertech, as you called it, is founded on these principles. Sure, every technocrat would welcome progress with open arms but it needs to be <i>stable progress</i>. A SoE/VA victory would sure have technomagick (and could be fun, I don't deny that), but the technomagick of those compared to the Technocracy is so distinct that it cannot be equally compared (and I <i>know</i> everybody in Mage is doing the same thing, the same magick and all that, but the conflict is still there and they literally kill each other on that perceived difference).<br /> <br /> Besides these distinctions, the reason the Technocracy sanitizes its hypertech before introduction is rooted, beyond any relation to Consensus, in a deep distrust of the Masses, If they didn't harbor such distrust, they wouldn't even exist, they would allow any paradigm to exist and any discovery to be championed and let the Masses figure it out for themselves. This distrust is so great, that among the possible antagonists proposed for technocratic characters in metaplot options in <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i> is the section titled <i>The Malignant Masses.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T08:36:13-07:00","id":1559352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559349#post1559349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't believe the Disparates are villain material. The Disparate Alliance in M20 was formed with the notion of survival, specifically to defend themselves and their communities against the Technocratic Pogrom, which in turn they believe to be corrupted by the Nephandi. They are close-minded, sure, but I don't believe they would want to vie for the reformating of Reality (although I cannot argument in favor for the Solificati, Wu Lung or Ahl-i-Batin on that front because of these groups notions of Global Ascension). They are written as the &quot;collateral damage&quot; of the Ascension War anyway, it wouldn't make sense for them to continue the very war that shattered their cultures. And their close-mindness is different from technocratic dogma, it sprouts from a place of guarding their communities (and their Reality Zones) from the encroaching of Technocratic Consensus, while the close-mindness of The Technocracy comes from a place of subjugating Reality in order to establish one and irrefutable Consensus, ignoring the diversity inherent to the very Reality they want to protect. The formation of the Alliance could very well make these groups more acceptable of each other's differences, just like it happened to the Traditions in the course of their history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was being sarcastic. Still, the narrow minded rigidity of the Technocracy is often found in both the Disparates and the Trads. The Trads especially the Hermetics who always get editorial contempt are working on the very problem that made them the threat the brought <b>The Order of Reason </b>together.<br /> <br /> Of course the thing is really the fury of the highly Romantic Paris arts community over the narrow mindedness of the Enlightenment. And the Disparates, like the Romantics, never notice their own close mindedness. So much of Mage really boils down to the original author's literature classes and the absurdities of the syllabuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T17:15:41-07:00","id":1559363,"title":"","content":"A digression, <b>Null Threat </b>is coming. None of the rest of the <b>Technocracy </b>can safely be told that. Does anyone else see an epic campaign were the <b>Void Engineers</b> tell the <b>Trads </b>and the <b>Disparates </b>about <b>Null Threat. </b>Leading to an epic team up to save the planet with comedy stylings based on keeping the <b>Technocracy </b>unaware of what's going on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T17:32:42-07:00","id":1559364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559363#post1559363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A digression, <b>Null Threat </b>is coming. None of the rest of the <b>Technocracy </b>can safely be told that. Does anyone else see an epic campaign were the <b>Void Engineers</b> tell the <b>Trads </b>and the <b>Disparates </b>about <b>Null Threat. </b>Leading to an epic team up to save the planet with comedy stylings based on keeping the <b>Technocracy </b>unaware of what's going on?</div> </div> </div> </div>[A number of Technocratic Union representatives are gather around a council table]<br /> <br /> VE Rep: This puts me in an unenviable position, but does everyone recall the Dimensional Anomaly, and how it cut off many of our... more longer-lived colleagues and superiors?<br /> <br /> [General grumblings to the affirmative among the council]<br /> <br /> VE Rep: Well, they're still around, after a fashion.<br /> <br /> Progenitor Rep: So when you say &quot;after a fashion&quot;...<br /> <br /> VE Rep: I mean that they underwent Dimensional Adaptation, and are no longer human as we understand it.<br /> <br /> ItX Rep: (Electronic simulated coughing noise)<br /> <br /> VE Rep: You fit in just fine, over there. I'm saying that they turned into Umbrood. And they think that we're the Reality Deviants.<br /> <br /> [Growing uproar]<br /> <br /> NWO Rep: And you were sitting on this since the subsidence of the DA?<br /> <br /> VE Rep: I'm afraid so. Look, they were in our stomping grounds first and foremost. They were our problem.<br /> <br /> [Uproar slowly gains in magnitude]<br /> <br /> Syndicate Rep: Well, as long as we're disclosing secrets...<br /> <br /> [Smash cut to the Syndicate Rep lying face down in a pool of blood, while the VE Rep brawls with the NWO, Progenitors, and ITx reps]<br /> <br /> Progenitor Rep: So we're in agreement... the last one standing leads the others in cleaning up these messes.<br /> <br /> NWO Rep: You should hand it over to us. You're obviously all too tired.<br /> <br /> ItX Rep: Speak for yourself, atavism.<br /> <br /> VE Rep: Momma didn't raise no quitter!<br /> <br /> [In the corner, a Glass Walker invited by the Progenitors stands dumbfounded]<br /> <br /> GW (internal monologue): Sweet Gaia it's strange to see this from the outside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T19:58:34-07:00","id":1559365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559364#post1559364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Smash cut to the Syndicate Rep lying face down in a pool of blood, while the VE Rep brawls with the NWO, Progenitors, and ITx reps]<br /> <br /> Progenitor Rep: So we're in agreement... the last one standing leads the others in cleaning up these messes.<br /> <br /> NWO Rep: You should hand it over to us. You're obviously all too tired.<br /> <br /> ItX Rep: Speak for yourself, atavism.<br /> <br /> VE Rep: Momma didn't raise no quitter!<br /> <br /> [In the corner, a Glass Walker invited by the Progenitors stands dumbfounded]<br /> <br /> GW (internal monologue): Sweet Gaia it's strange to see this from the outside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't expecting<i> this</i> in the end of this thread... I like the Glass Walker mention though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T20:19:22-07:00","id":1559366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559364#post1559364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [In the corner, a Glass Walker invited by the Progenitors stands dumbfounded]<br /> <br /> GW (internal monologue): Sweet Gaia it's strange to see this from the outside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you did there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T04:46:31-07:00","id":1559371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559350#post1559350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on how you define the state of Consensus in your game. In M20, 3 scenarios are proposed for the ST: 1) <b>The Technocracy Won: </b>the pervasive belief in technology subjugate any mystical paradigm and it would be something like you said, which would really cast doubt in the Technocracy's good intentions in not giving their hypertech to the Masses; 2) <b>Technocratic Belief Dominates Certain Parts of the World</b>: this one punch holes in the notion of a Technocratic Consensus and the existence of Reality Zones would make the Technocracy be more careful with when, where, and how to introduce hypertech in regions of the world where it would generate Paradox/Rejection/Correction; 3) <b>Reality's in Flux: </b>this scenario laughs at the idea of any Consensus, giving the opportunity to make vulgar magick into coincidental magick and the opposite for ceratin kinds of technology. <hr /><br /> Another thing I don't think is accurate is to frame the conflict between the Traditions (or any mystic Mage) and the Technocracy as an issue of the existence of technology. Since <i>Guide to The Traditions</i>, technology is said to be present in the ranks of the Council, even beyond the halls of the Society of Ether and the Virtual Adepts. The presence of technology in the Traditions is even more pervasive by the time of M20 in <i>Lore of The Traditions</i>, even being a major source of inner conflict in some groups like the Verbena. The distinction between the Traditions and Technocracy is not one of &quot;Technology Bad vs Technology Good&quot; (if it was sure, let the VAs and Etherites have at it), but of what paradigms are <i>allowed</i> to exist and which ones should shape Consensus. The Technocracy is not merely the party of technology, but the party of Order, Stability and above all <i>Control</i>. The Science of the SoE and VAs is rooted in technology/technomagick, but is utterly anathema to the Technocracy because is not &quot;ordely&quot;, stable and thus it cannot be properly controlled. The need for sanitization before any introduction of technocratic hypertech, as you called it, is founded on these principles. Sure, every technocrat would welcome progress with open arms but it needs to be <i>stable progress</i>. A SoE/VA victory would sure have technomagick (and could be fun, I don't deny that), but the technomagick of those compared to the Technocracy is so distinct that it cannot be equally compared (and I <i>know</i> everybody in Mage is doing the same thing, the same magick and all that, but the conflict is still there and they literally kill each other on that perceived difference).<br /> <br /> Besides these distinctions, the reason the Technocracy sanitizes its hypertech before introduction is rooted, beyond any relation to Consensus, in a deep distrust of the Masses, If they didn't harbor such distrust, they wouldn't even exist, they would allow any paradigm to exist and any discovery to be championed and let the Masses figure it out for themselves. This distrust is so great, that among the possible antagonists proposed for technocratic characters in metaplot options in <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i> is the section titled <i>The Malignant Masses.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer the idea that Technocratic belief dominates certain areas of the world, which allows for the existence of Reality Zones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T19:39:44-07:00","id":1559440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559330#post1559330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as a side note: I tend to get a lot of pushback on this, but it's been my headcanon that the Syndicate is the Convention of economic systems, not just capitalist ones. Indeed, if they are tied to the value of human endeavor rather than money itself, it makes sense that they would be. I think they've done a at least some experimenting around with planned and communist economies and they may do so again in the future. But as I said, that's mostly headcanon, so feel free to disregard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one reason why you get that pushback is that that doesn't leave any room for anyone <i>else </i>to focus on economic systems. Which canonically isn't true: there's a faction within the Etherites who champion socialism and post-scarcity economies. <br /> <br /> But also because of the Technocracy's &quot;One True Way&quot; mentality. &quot;The Convention of all economic systems, even mutually exclusive ones&quot; is remarkably open-minded for a Convention. I <i>could </i>see them saying something like &quot;communism? Yeah, we experimented with it a bit in the 20th century. It didn't work out.&quot; They're not trying it <i>now, </i>because they're convinced it's unworkable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T08:35:38-07:00","id":1559455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559440#post1559440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one reason why you get that pushback is that that doesn't leave any room for anyone <i>else </i>to focus on economic systems. Which canonically isn't true: there's a faction within the Etherites who champion socialism and post-scarcity economies.<br /> <br /> But also because of the Technocracy's &quot;One True Way&quot; mentality. &quot;The Convention of all economic systems, even mutually exclusive ones&quot; is remarkably open-minded for a Convention. I <i>could </i>see them saying something like &quot;communism? Yeah, we experimented with it a bit in the 20th century. It didn't work out.&quot; They're not trying it <i>now, </i>because they're convinced it's unworkable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so open minded as that. More like 'all economic systems that can be used to optimize, harness, or exploiting human endeavor'. Also, just because they have several options doesn't mean they don't have a preference or that they can't be at odds with other factions. There's still plenty of room for other mages to disagree about the best way of coordinating human endeavor, or disagree for moral or philosophical reasons.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T12:17:48-07:00","id":1559460,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty much with Ramnnesis on this one. Even though the Convention books do present Syndicate as being about personal wealth, I think they are more interesting as being about setting up the system as promoting Quintessence as Value to be shared, grown, or taken through mediums of exchange than as just wanting the wealth for themselves as dirty Capitalists.<br /> Capitalism may be either the most efficient way of doing this, or may even be a Sleeper representation of their higher economic magic, in the same way Sleeper religions are not a one for one match with Chorus or Batini paradigms. <br /> The Etherites are more pushing a utopia where work done generates and distributes Quintessence. The value of an item is the work put into it rather than the end sale or resale price. Intrinsic value instead of defined by exchange. The difference is as much about what shapes and defines reality as about mundane economic models.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12269-heilong","name":"Heilong","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T01:56:06-07:00","id":1559474,"title":"","content":"Something which just occurred to me that I think bares mentioning is that capitalism is not merely an avenue to financial success. It is a major foundation behind how the Syndicate's magic even functions in the first place. Capitalism is part of their paradigm, so they can not simply abandon or tone it down, without radically altering their perception and understanding of <i>&quot;enlightened science.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T08:26:21-07:00","id":1559480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559474#post1559474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something which just occurred to me that I think bares mentioning is that capitalism is not merely an avenue to financial success. It is a major foundation behind how the Syndicate's magic even functions in the first place. Capitalism is part of their paradigm, so they can not simply abandon or tone it down, without radically altering their perception and understanding of <i>&quot;enlightened science.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The foundation of the <b>High Guild </b>was the belief that merchants were more than just peasants for the nobility to order around. They might have dressed it up philosophically but the wealthy merchants didn't see themselves as inferior to the nobility. The Merchants had a point. They were often far better educated, far more sophisticated in taste, more refined in manners, and vastly more capable than the nobles. <br /> <br /> Capitalism, a term invented by a man that wanted to abolish it, was never just about wealth. It was also about power and respect. Wealth, power, influence and status matter to the <b>Syndicate, </b>Capitalism is someone else's word. I doubt it's the hill they would die on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T14:29:10-07:00","id":1559489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559480#post1559480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The foundation of the <b>High Guild </b>was the belief that merchants were more than just peasants for the nobility to order around. They might have dressed it up philosophically but the wealthy merchants didn't see themselves as inferior to the nobility. The Merchants had a point. They were often far better educated, far more sophisticated in taste, more refined in manners, and vastly more capable than the nobles.<br /> <br /> Capitalism, a term invented by a man that wanted to abolish it, was never just about wealth. It was also about power and respect. Wealth, power, influence and status matter to the <b>Syndicate, </b>Capitalism is someone else's word. I doubt it's the hill they would die on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a member of the nobility had nothing to do with how capable of educated you were. It was the perceived notion that your very bloodline was innately superior to those of the lower class.<br /> <br /> The Sidhe are the embodiment of the 'Divine Right to Rule' ideology. They don't need to prove their worth to anyone, because the very gods themselves have ordained them worthy. To challenge that notion is an act of blasphemy, which is why it was so difficult for them to accept the notion of treating commoners like equals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T14:36:32-07:00","id":1559490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559489#post1559489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being a member of the nobility had nothing to do with how capable of educated you were. It was the perceived notion that your very bloodline was innately superior to those of the lower class.<br /> <br /> The Sidhe are the embodiment of the 'Divine Right to Rule' ideology. They don't need to prove their worth to anyone, because the very gods themselves have ordained them worthy. To challenge that notion is an act of blasphemy, which is why it was so difficult for them to accept the notion of treating commoners like equals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And now the Syndicate has created a world were the rich are as toxic as the nobility were while being vastly harder to romantize. All the same pain with less fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T17:48:41-07:00","id":1559493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559490#post1559490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. And now the Syndicate has created a world were the rich are as toxic as the nobility were while being vastly harder to romantize. All the same pain with less fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's frustrating to realize that the ultra rich, financial elite never actually seem to face any real consequences for their screw ups. No matter how many thousands, millions, or even billions of dollars they lose, they SOMEHOW always seem to have enough remaining to go right back to doing the same crap they were doing before. It's almost as if their wealth is infinite, since they never seem to run out!<br /> <br /> <br /> Nor do they actually go to prison when outed for a crime. Or, sure, they receive public ridicule and outrage for their poor behavior. But I can't remember the last time I've heard of a billionaire actually being sentenced to do time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T18:59:52-07:00","id":1559494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559493#post1559493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's frustrating to realize that the ultra rich, financial elite never actually seem to face any real consequences for their screw ups. No matter how many thousands, millions, or even billions of dollars they lose, they SOMEHOW always seem to have enough remaining to go right back to doing the same crap they were doing before. It's almost as if their wealth is infinite, since they never seem to run out!<br /> <br /> <br /> Nor do they actually go to prison when outed for a crime. Or, sure, they receive public ridicule and outrage for their poor behavior. But I can't remember the last time I've heard of a billionaire actually being sentenced to do time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, but there's a defense keyed right into the rich and ultra-rich being &quot;unsuited&quot; for prison time (&quot;affluenza&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T07:24:18-07:00","id":1559502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559494#post1559494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not only that, but there's a defense keyed right into the rich and ultra-rich being &quot;unsuited&quot; for prison time (&quot;affluenza&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Affluenza also sounds like an artificially engineered Etherite disease that targets only the rich.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T11:42:15-07:00","id":1559505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559502#post1559502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Affluenza also sounds like an artificially engineered Etherite disease that targets only the rich.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the early 20th century all sorts of people were whining about how soft and decadent people were getting. As time progressed these attacks were targeted at the working class and the poor. As John Kenneth Galbraith (a wise economist your teachers hid from you) pointed out in the early 1960s the &quot;poor have gotten the disease of affluence without ever being affluent.&quot;<br /> <br /> Either Galbraith or Michael Harrington (a wonderful radical who was skilled at getting people to see the clothes had no emperor) coined the term &quot;Affluenza&quot; to mock right-wingers who claimed we were &quot;spoiling&quot; the poor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T16:42:05-07:00","id":1559509,"title":"","content":"Not the first time an insult has been weaponized by the target. Nor the first time wealth or power made a good point ineffectual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12269-heilong","name":"Heilong","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T17:34:51-07:00","id":1559510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559505#post1559505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the early 20th century all sorts of people were whining about how soft and decadent people were getting. As time progressed these attacks were targeted at the working class and the poor. As John Kenneth Galbraith (a wise economist your teachers hid from you) pointed out in the early 1960s the &quot;poor have gotten the disease of affluence without ever being affluent.&quot;<br /> <br /> Either Galbraith or Michael Harrington (a wonderful radical who was skilled at getting people to see the clothes had no emperor) coined the term &quot;Affluenza&quot; to mock right-wingers who claimed we were &quot;spoiling&quot; the poor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I\u2019ve heard the term before, though as I recall the use was completely different in the 00\u2019s. More to do with an unhappiness and despair in those who seem to have everything. <br /> <br /> But it\u2019s really easy to see an Etherite grabbing the word and putting it to a more direct use.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T19:30:32-07:00","id":1559513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559494#post1559494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not only that, but there's a defense keyed right into the rich and ultra-rich being &quot;unsuited&quot; for prison time (&quot;affluenza&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, I'm not advocating for communism / socialism, since they're even more dysfunctional.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying that it's gotten disheartening when I continuously see videos pop up in my recommended feed about how badly so-and-so company has fucked up this week, only to have the world carry on as if nothing has changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-20T14:02:42-07:00","id":1559536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559502#post1559502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Affluenza also sounds like an artificially engineered Etherite disease that targets only the rich.</div> </div> </div> </div>We could only be so fortunate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify, I'm not advocating for communism / socialism, since they're even more dysfunctional.</div> </div> </div> </div>More that they don't solve pre-existing problems inherently. But then, neither will capitalism. Gulags were not a thing that commies made, for example; they date back to Tsarist Russia. They became the answer of &quot;what to do to people who don't agree with us&quot; because they were there and everyone around was sort of conditioned to accept that this is how things are done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm just saying that it's gotten disheartening when I continuously see videos pop up in my recommended feed about how badly so-and-so company has fucked up this week, only to have the world carry on as if nothing has changed. </div> </div> </div>The least realistic part of thriller fiction is when disclosure of dirty laundry causes changes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T19:06:23-07:00","id":1561403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559341#post1559341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno. The VAs kinda <i>did</i> win in RL. Like, the ideas and movements that the VAs are a riff on are both hugely influential and powerful in the present. The difference comes from the books wanting the VAs to remain cool cyberpunks, rather than the kinds of people who want to talk about race IQ stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh. Don't get me started on this. Speaking as a computer guy/information scientist, I have never met any programmers, hackers, or anyone otherwise involved in &quot;VA jobs&quot; who are racist. My father, who has been programming since the era of FORTRAN and COBOL, also has not. The open source community which is represented by the VA still operates on the egalitarian ethos it always operated on. Tech Bros are not us, but the Syndicate guys above us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T13:18:59-07:00","id":1561428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1561403#post1561403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The open source community which is represented by the VA still operates on the egalitarian ethos it always operated on.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's drawing on much broader California ideology stuff. That includes open source stuff, but it also includes the tech bros, and frankly, the latter are far more influential.<br /> <br /> I mean, just read <i>Lore of the Traditions.</i> There's very little on providing open source software to sleepers. There's 'cryptocurrency manipulation', and vaguely Rationalist ideas about AGI.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tech Bros are not us, but the Syndicate guys above us. </div> </div> </div>Okay, but we get little indication of that. Like, if the VAs were struggling with large parts of their membership selling out to the Syndicate, that'd be great. That'd be really cool.<br /> <br /> The series did lean that way with <i>Iteration: X Revised</i>, but I don't think there's been further development of that idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T23:21:32-07:00","id":1561503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559343#post1559343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because they read the book, realized the Doctor Moreau was a satirical critique of God in Genesis and decided medical research was less cruel and more rewarding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take your word for it, as I never read the book or saw the entire movie.<br /> <br /> But I was thinking something more along the lines of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n6jPe-0qPyk\" target=\"_blank\">this game.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T09:33:51-07:00","id":1561654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1559363#post1559363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A digression, <b>Null Threat </b>is coming. None of the rest of the <b>Technocracy </b>can safely be told that. Does anyone else see an epic campaign were the <b>Void Engineers</b> tell the <b>Trads </b>and the <b>Disparates </b>about <b>Null Threat. </b>Leading to an epic team up to save the planet with comedy stylings based on keeping the <b>Technocracy </b>unaware of what's going on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd view Threat Null's victory as a final <i>&quot;fuck you&quot;</i> to the Technocratic Union, if it came down to it.<br /> <br /> Something along the lines of <i>&quot;Why aren't you smiling Technocrat? This is what you wanted! A world of secular rationalism, ruled by science and technology. No magic, no supernaturals, just a universe made by humans, for humans. Oh, I know why, it's because your new machine god decided that emotions were illogical!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, now you have all of eternity to experience life as a genetically perfect, hivemind consciousness. Without a single independent thought in your head.&quot; *</i>flips the metaphorical table and leaves the Tellurian.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T14:29:45-07:00","id":1561659,"title":"","content":"We have first to be clear if we're talking pre-GttT or post-GttT Syndicate. The whole Union is a completely different thing in each. Old T is the Conspiracy Behind the System, the villains who deliberately keep the world being how it is.<br /> <br /> From Guide to the Technocracy onward they're a conspiracy with a <i>plan</i>, but not with the whole picture or full control. This distinction is really important, because this Technocracy is NOT the reason why the world is the way it is, how much it's their doing is debatable, and each of the Conventions changes from Secret Masters to Ideals Gone Wrong.<br /> <br /> Next, identify where we run a risk of conflating things, and define them clearly.<br /> <br /> The Revised Syndicate os not about <b>Capitalism</b> but about <i><b>Capital</b></i>. An important distinction and yes, we'll use Marx's definitions because they are the scientific definitions we have:<br /> <br /> <b>Capital is not money</b>. Capital is <i>money as the engine of production</i>. This is a very new thing in history, and is at the center of Capitalism, but isn't limited to Capitalism.<br /> <br /> Question: what you need in the first place to start to make something with economic value? The answer to this question is the engine of production of a society.<br /> <br /> Before the Industrial Revolution it changed with time and place, but the common denominator<br /> was land control (it still plays a huge role). In the late Middle Ages you could be rich as fuck, without land you couldn't do shit and no one would sell you land just for money if they weren't in a desperate situation.<br /> <br /> Money already existed. Commerce already existed. But Capital didn't. Nobles with control over land could lend or take this control as the primary means to make things happen. Give an artisan a shop, give the right places to those who produce what they need and so forth.<br /> <br /> So the transformation brought by the Industry that both birthed Capitalism and the Syndicate proper was not the system of relationships and power we call Capitalism (it has additional roots), but Capital: production became so fast and distribution so easy that you can, in fact, just buy your way into establishing a business.<br /> <br /> It's so powerful and complete that today we have this weird problem where we can't easily understand Capital because <i>we can't wrap our minds over the notion of its absence</i> to have a contrast to compare.<br /> <br /> And I think this is our first point to define: is my proposal coherent? Is the Syndicate about the specific system, the mere idea of money, or the basic framework where money itself is the medium to establish production?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T15:04:44-07:00","id":1561661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1561659#post1561659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have first to be clear if we're talking pre-GttT or post-GttT Syndicate. The whole Union is a completely different thing in each. Old T is the Conspiracy Behind the System, the villains who deliberately keep the world being how it is.<br /> <br /> From Guide to the Technocracy onward they're a conspiracy with a <i>plan</i>, but not with the whole picture or full control. This distinction is really important, because this Technocracy is NOT the reason why the world is the way it is, how much it's their doing is debatable, and each of the Conventions changes from Secret Masters to Ideals Gone Wrong.<br /> <br /> Next, identify where we run a risk of conflating things, and define them clearly.<br /> <br /> The Revised Syndicate os not about <b>Capitalism</b> but about <i><b>Capital</b></i>. An important distinction and yes, we'll use Marx's definitions because they are the scientific definitions we have:<br /> <br /> <b>Capital is not money</b>. Capital is <i>money as the engine of production</i>. This is a very new thing in history, and is at the center of Capitalism, but isn't limited to Capitalism.<br /> <br /> Question: what you need in the first place to start to make something with economic value? The answer to this question is the engine of production of a society.<br /> <br /> Before the Industrial Revolution it changed with time and place, but the common denominator<br /> was land control (it still plays a huge role). In the late Middle Ages you could be rich as fuck, without land you couldn't do shit and no one would sell you land just for money if they weren't in a desperate situation.<br /> <br /> Money already existed. Commerce already existed. But Capital didn't. Nobles with control over land could lend or take this control as the primary means to make things happen. Give an artisan a shop, give the right places to those who produce what they need and so forth.<br /> <br /> So the transformation brought by the Industry that both birthed Capitalism and the Syndicate proper was not the system of relationships and power we call Capitalism (it has additional roots), but Capital: production became so fast and distribution so easy that you can, in fact, just buy your way into establishing a business.<br /> <br /> It's so powerful and complete that today we have this weird problem where we can't easily understand Capital because <i>we can't wrap our minds over the notion of its absence</i> to have a contrast to compare.<br /> <br /> And I think this is our first point to define: is my proposal coherent? Is the Syndicate about the specific system, the mere idea of money, or the basic framework where money itself is the medium to establish production?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not identical to my suggestion about the Handelsgeist (the spirit of peaceful and mutually beneficial trade) but closer than not. And it certainly goes with the idea of &quot;productive use of time.&quot; <br /> <br /> All in all, Monteparnas you've summed up the ideas put out about the Syndicate in their Convention Books and substantially improved on clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T08:51:35-07:00","id":1561685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1561659#post1561659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Revised Syndicate os not about <b>Capitalism</b> but about <i><b>Capital</b></i>. An important distinction and yes, we'll use Marx's definitions because they are the scientific definitions we have:<br /> <br /> <b>Capital is not money</b>. Capital is <i>money as the engine of production</i>. This is a very new thing in history, and is at the center of Capitalism, but isn't limited to Capitalism.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What would be an example of an economic system that is a &quot;Capital without Capitalism&quot;? And, if the essence of the Syndicate is Capital and not Capitalism, could said economic system be a model for a &quot;redeemed Syndicate&quot;?<br /> <br /> Would the concept of Infinite Shareholder Returns mentioned in <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i> be a kind of &quot;socially-owned Capital&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T13:06:15-07:00","id":1561734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559296-is-there-a-way-to-rehabilitate-the-syndicate?p=1561685#post1561685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would be an example of an economic system that is a &quot;Capital without Capitalism&quot;? And, if the essence of the Syndicate is Capital and not Capitalism, could said economic system be a model for a &quot;redeemed Syndicate&quot;?<br /> <br /> Would the concept of Infinite Shareholder Returns mentioned in <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i> be a kind of &quot;socially-owned Capital&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any system where you organize production by paying people, can pay to overcome obstacles and credit exists is based on Capital.<br /> <br /> Money is a language. It translates Value. It isn't value, but makes value communicable through time and space.<br /> <br /> It isn't new. It's older than written records and we have some artifacts pointing that maybe a form of money is at least as old as the Genus Homo, and maybe present in animals without our noticing.<br /> <br /> The game focus on the idea of commodifying, but the notion that anything can be bought isn't inherently dehumanizing. It simply means that everything has value, and as such this value can be translated through money. Also everything can be negotiated, but negotiation is how relationships happen.<br /> <br /> So saying &quot;money buys everything&quot; isn't the same as saying &quot;money IS everything&quot;, or &quot;money is THE ONLY WAY to buy things&quot;. Instead, think of it as &quot;everything that has value can have this value recognized through a price&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is how you recognize someone's work is worth it, and their time and effort deserves a reward. With this you recognize the resources someone needs to live, and stipulate a minimum wage that shouldn't be &quot;deserved&quot; because it isn't about reward, it's about basic human dignity.<br /> <br /> Without Capital we make do with other things. Someone still controls whatever is needed for production and people still toil to get their fill, but we can't price everything and can't price the most important things.<br /> <br /> Ever since the Industrial Revolution we haven't gotten a single system that isn't partially based on Capital, and those who ditched it partially regretted later. Because you're not ditching the exploitation, you're ditching the language of value.<br /> <br /> Capital can be socially owned. Shares do that, but through an exploitative system the real Left wrongly refuses to engage. Socialized companies effectively work by socializing Capital. Many grassroots organizations that make life bearable for the downtrodden do that even if they don't notice.<br /> <br /> So, if you picture a Mage that gets powerful by direct control of any particular resource, and while they may get wealthy with it and use the wealth for Magic, they have a clear source for their power and wealth, this is a Money Mage of any faction.<br /> <br /> But if you picture a Mage that uses money as the language of Production, Resources and Labor, the Mediator that enables everything, and whose Magic is based on this shared medium rather than its source or its final use, this is the Syndicate \u2013 even if they're talking about socializing resources, labor laws and production as a collective achievement rather than individual merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}